# SourceUp CRM — Cursor Rules

## Stack (match exactly — do not introduce new libraries)

### Backend
- Runtime: Node.js with ES Modules ("type": "module") — always import/export, never require()
- Framework: Express 5
- Database: MongoDB via Mongoose 9
- Auth: jsonwebtoken 9 + bcrypt 6 + HttpOnly cookies
- File uploads: Multer 2
- Email: Nodemailer (SMTP)
- PDF export: pdfkit
- Excel export: exceljs
- Validation: custom Validation.js utility (same pattern as BMS-APP)
- Error handling: AsyncHandler + ApiError + ApiResponse utilities (same as BMS-APP)
- Environment: dotenv — .env.local for dev, .env for production

### Frontend
- Framework: React 19 + Vite 8
- Routing: React Router DOM v7
- HTTP client: Axios — one shared instance with baseURL and withCredentials: true
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v4 (Vite plugin — NOT PostCSS) + custom CSS variables
- State management: React Context only — no Redux, no Zustand
- Icons: lucide-react
- Animations: motion (Framer Motion v13)
- UI components: shadcn/ui + @base-ui/react
- Fonts: @fontsource-variable/geist

### Deployment
- Backend: Render
- Frontend: Vercel
- Dev proxy: Vite proxies /api/v1/* → http://localhost:3000

---

## Backend Conventions

### File naming
- Controllers: PascalCase.controller.js (e.g. Lead.controller.js)
- Routes: PascalCase.routes.js (e.g. Lead.routes.js)
- Middleware: PascalCase.middleware.js
- Models: PascalCase.schema.js
- Utils: PascalCase.js

### Every controller must use this structure
```js
import { AsyncHandler } from "../Utils/AsyncHandler.js";
import { ApiError } from "../Utils/ApiError.js";
import { ApiResponse } from "../Utils/ApiResponse.js";

const myHandler = AsyncHandler(async (req, res) => {
  // 1. Validate input
  // 2. DB operation
  // 3. Respond with ApiResponse
});
RBAC middleware — apply on every protected route
js

// requireRole checks req.user.role against allowed roles
router.route("/leads").get(VerifyJWT, requireRole("sales", "manager", "superadmin"), getLeads);
Cookie options — always use this exact pattern
js

const cookieOptions = {
  httpOnly: true,
  secure: process.env.NODE_ENV === "production",
  sameSite: process.env.NODE_ENV === "production" ? "none" : "lax",
};
ES Modules — always include .js extension in imports
js

import { Lead } from "../MongoDB/Models/Lead.schema.js";
Never use try/catch inside AsyncHandler — let errors propagate
Exception: OAuth-style redirect flows may use try/catch for per-case redirects